# Project Requirements Document (PRD)

## 1. Project Overview

Vitoria-Gasteiz City Council needs a single, web-based platform to manage all aspects of its urban feline colonies (linked to expediente **2026/CO_ASUM/0013**). Right now, data on colonies, individual cats, veterinary interventions (TNR: Trap-Neuter-Return), incidents, inspections and collaborators are scattered across spreadsheets, paper forms and siloed systems. This causes delays, data inconsistencies and poor transparency.

We will build a modular, responsive web app (desktop, tablet, mobile) that centralizes: colony maps, cat census, health records, CER program metrics, incident logging, inspection templates, collaborator credentials, adoptions, communications and automatic reporting. Success means a fully deployable, EU-hosted monolith (2-year contract, plus optional 2-year extension), compliant with GDPR, PCAP and Ayuntamiento pliegos, ready for production (not a prototype).

