## 3. User Flow

A typical user arrives at the login page, authenticates via Better Auth (email + password, 2FA optional). After login, they land on a **Dashboard** showing summary cards (e.g., active colonies, pending incidents, CER success rate). A left-hand navigation panel lists modules: Colonies, Map, Cats, Health, CER, Incidents, Inspections, Collaborators, Adoptions, Messages, Reports and Settings.

From the map view, a field inspector on mobile taps the map to register a new feeding point or incident using automatic GPS capture and optional photo upload. Back at their desk, a municipal technician clicks the **Cats** module to open an individual cat’s record, update its sterilization date, attach a health PDF certificate stub, then marks it as adopted. The user then generates an annual report (Excel/PDF), downloads it, and logs out. Every action is audited.

